<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Late Bronze Age collapse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> · Also known as Bronze Age Collapse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> collapse was a period of widespread destruction and political breakdown in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> around 1200 BCE. Its causes are debated and probably combined drought, famine, migrations including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a>, internal unrest and disrupted trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> disintegrated in this period, and the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> survived but entered a long decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age-collapse.jpg" alt="Late Bronze Age collapse" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexikoua · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bronze_Age_End.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
